447 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (The study details the design and testing of an electric bicycle powered by a 300 W PEM fuel cell with metal hydride hydrogen storage, managed by a custom microcontroller. The system achieved 35% efficiency and 1.35 km per gram of hydrogen. Low-pressure metal hydride storage enhanced safety, and tests confirmed stable, reliable performance. [3])
/E (The study details the design and testing of an electric bicycle powered by a 300 W PEM fuel cell with metal hydride hydrogen storage, managed by a custom microcontroller. The system achieved 35% efficiency and 1.35 km per gram of hydrogen. Low-pressure metal hydride storage enhanced safety, and tests confirmed stable, reliable performance. [3])
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
